§§ `Clause 10 — PVI's liability`

-- On early termination PVI's liability ends at once, including for medical costs or any
-- consequence arising after termination, even if the insured event arose while the certificate
-- was in force. On expiry at the end of the term, liability ends likewise; PVI stays liable on
-- claims for events that arose in the term, except for costs and consequences arising after the
-- certificate ended. The last day of liability is the end date of the term, or the day before
-- the date of early termination (fork F8).
