@ref PVI Rules Part I clause 10 (src:169-189)
GIVEN cert IS A `A certificate`
GIVETH A DATE
`clause 10 — the last day of PVI's liability under` cert MEANS
    CONSIDER cert's `date of early termination`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN cert's `this period`'s `end date`
    WHEN JUST t  THEN IF   t MINUS 1 AT MOST cert's `this period`'s `end date`
                      THEN t MINUS 1
                      ELSE cert's `this period`'s `end date`

@ref PVI Rules Part I clause 10 (src:169-174, 176-189)
GIVEN cert IS A `A certificate`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 10 — a day within PVI's liability under` cert `:` `the day` MEANS
        `the day` AT LEAST cert's `this period`'s `start date`
    AND `the day` AT MOST `clause 10 — the last day of PVI's liability under` cert

§§ `Clause 11 — The insured person's responsibilities`

-- Duties to declare honestly and pay the premium on time, to comply with the Rules, to take
-- reasonable steps to limit the consequences of an insured event, to notify "as early as possible"
-- circumstances that may lead to or aggravate a claim, and to be honest in declaring the event and
-- its documents. None carries a deadline the Rules state; they are carried inert.
