--
-- Dishonesty: PVI may cancel the certificate and/or refuse part or all of the money "depending on
-- the gravity of the breach", and the premium paid is not refunded. The extent is PVI's
-- discretion with no criterion (finding X10); the encoding records the permission and the refund
-- the clause states. LAW: Art. 22(2) of the Law on Insurance Business (aid line 543-551) requires
-- the insurer that cancels for intentionally false information to refund the premium less
-- reasonable costs (fork F13).
